# ============================================================
# CHARACTERIZATION OF TRYPTIC, SEMI-TRYPTIC AND NON-TRYPTIC
# lncRNA-DERIVED PEPTIDES
# ============================================================
#
# This script compares peptide sequence features among three
# trypticity classes:
#
#   - Tryptic
#   - Semi-tryptic
#   - Non-tryptic
#
# INPUT REQUIREMENT
# -----------------
# The input Excel file must contain:
#   1. A peptide-sequence column.
#   2. A classification column indicating whether each peptide is
#      tryptic, semi-tryptic or non-tryptic.
#   3. Optionally, a reported peptide-length column.
#
# Common classification labels are standardized automatically.
# All three classes are retained and compared throughout the analysis.
# The script also reports the most frequent amino-acid pairs and
# triplets specifically within the non-tryptic group.
#
# Main analyses
# -------------
#   - peptide-length comparison
#   - amino-acid composition by class
#   - amino-acid group composition by class
#   - sequence-complexity comparison
#   - overlapping amino-acid pairs and triplets
#   - physicochemical-property comparison
#
# Statistical approach
# --------------------
# Global comparisons use Kruskal-Wallis tests. Pairwise comparisons
# use Wilcoxon rank-sum tests with Benjamini-Hochberg correction.
#
# Author: Maria Mulet
# ============================================================

